<title>SWITZERLAND: Nokia's Maillefer sees outlook improving slowly.</title>
<headline>Nokia's Maillefer sees outlook improving slowly.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nokia's subsidiary Maillefer said it saw profits in 1997 returning towards the 1995 level and expected clear improvements in 1998.</p>
<p>The company said the outlook for 1997 was much more favourable than last year because of the Swiss franc's weakness and the strength of the dollar.</p>
<p>The company said it expected profits to improve in 1998 but gave no forecasts.</p>
<p>&quot;The relative weakness of the Swiss franc against other currencies will have a generally positive impact on Nokia-Maillefer's operations,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
